{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The overlap occurred in the exploration: after one dropped `TimeoutNow`, the leader remained in joint state through transfer timeout and the reliable suffix. The control exited automatically; a later ordinary proposal also enabled exit in the overlap case. This is bounded non-completion, not yet a liveness finding.\n\nI also found an observation discrepancy: `Status().Config` uses `Config.Clone`, which omits `AutoLeave`. I’ll retain that separate lead and use the live configuration field for continuation diagnostics.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > obligation.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json')); c=r['candidates'][0];q=c['question']\nq['unknowns']=['A fixed check must establish a repeatable suffix from behavior-determining state, external tick/message schedule and drained queues; finite elapsed ticks alone do not exclude future automatic continuation.']\nq['counterevidence'].append('Exploration shows an unrelated ordinary proposal allows exit, confirming a remaining application-progress trigger; this does not show that callers owe that proposal.')\nq['disposition']='ready_for_check'\nclaim='O-implicit-exit-continuation'\nss=['s-implicit-contract','s-autoleave-owner','s-apply-reset','s-authority','s-abort-transfer','s-propose','s-advance','s-config']\np=dict(action='obligation',candidate_id=c['id'],question=q,rationale='Ground the implementation-owned implicit exit responsibility separately from bounded waiting. The next fixed check will look for a closed, repeatable service suffix with an uncompleted exit, not impose a made-up tick deadline.',sources=[dict(id='s-config-clone',file='tracker/tracker.go',start_line=94,end_line=112,kind='code_observation')],obligation=dict(id=claim,kind='obligation',concern='bounded_liveness',description='For a committed and applied implicit joint transition, Raft must retain automatic continuation to the final configuration when a leader and both quorums are available and caller-required ticking, transport, persistence and application continue. A rejected internal exit proposal during a transient leadership transfer must not leave the transition permanently dependent on an unrelated new client proposal after the transfer has ended.',source_ids=ss,scope=dict(description='Implicit joint exit with the current leader retained as a voter, a transient failed transfer, no ongoing failures and fair servicing of all implementation-requested work.',assumptions=['Configuration entry is genuinely committed and applied through the normal interface.','Transport may lose finitely many messages, then delivers all generated messages; local Ready work is processed reliably in order.','Stable available leader and sufficient incoming/outgoing voters; no infinite elections or failed storage.','No obligation for a fresh unrelated user command or manually proposed explicit exit is imposed on implicit-transition callers.'],excluded=['No numeric deadline for exit.','No claim that configuration proposals must be admitted initially.','No crash/restart, Byzantine behavior, explicit joint transitions or arbitrary membership changes.','No claim of consensus safety failure or measured downstream availability outage.']),pending=[],grounding=dict(source_ids=ss,expectation_ids=['s-implicit-contract','s-autoleave-owner'],derivation='ConfChangeTransitionJointImplicit specifies that raft transitions out automatically by proposing a zero change, whereas JointExplicit assigns that proposal to the application. tracker.Config.AutoLeave repeats that ownership when possible. appliedTo implements the automatic proposal and documents transfer rejection plus an expected later advance. Generic proposal retry duties do not transfer this internal automatic task to the caller. The responsibility is eventual continuation under available quorums, not completion after a fixed number of ticks.',applicability='Actual committed/applied implicit transition and fully serviced stable-leader suffix after a finite failed transfer. A violation requires a closed non-progress execution suffix or equivalently sourced proof that required future triggers cannot occur, beyond finite non-completion.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['A successful leadership change or later applied ordinary entry can initiate exit; those rescue paths do not establish automatic continuation in a stable idle workload.'])),bindings=[dict(id='bind-autoexit',material_id='s-apply-reset',symbol='(*raft).appliedTo',start_line=740,end_line=767,description='Consumes applied progress and AutoLeave to attempt the internal empty proposal, including the transfer rejection branch.',pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claim,source_ids=['s-implicit-contract','s-autoleave-owner'],rationale='This is the implementation-owned initiator of the specified automatic transition.')]),dict(id='bind-transfer-timeout',material_id='s-authority',symbol='(*raft).tickHeartbeat',start_line=862,end_line=889,description='Timeout of the interfering transfer under regularly supplied ticks.',pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claim,source_ids=['s-implicit-contract','s-abort-transfer'],rationale='Clears the temporary proposal-suppression context; whether automatic work remains enabled is the discriminator.')])],feedback=dict(ref_ids=[c['id'],'7787ec32a33f4ae0a2f558ac34428ecd','s-apply-reset','s-abort-transfer','s-config-clone','s-status-copy'],answered='Exploration 7787ec32a33f4ae0a2f558ac34428ecd executed a three-node public-API history: implicit removal entry index 5 was committed and applied; transfer target 2 was installed before Advance; one emitted TimeoutNow was dropped. At timeout and after thirty additional reliably delivered tick rounds, leader 1 remained term 2 with commit/applied/last index 5 and outgoing count 3. Network queue, leader Ready, storage/apply pending work were empty in emitted diagnostics. The no-transfer control exited at index 6; later ordinary proposal in the overlap case enabled exit at index 7. Public Status AutoLeave=false is not evidence of live AutoLeave loss: getStatus calls Config.Clone, whose returned literal omits AutoLeave. Preserve this independent copy discrepancy and use live fields when checking continuation.',remaining=['Formal execution must follow fixed inputs and an independent correlated predicate; exploration is not Evidence.','Full recurrence needs all relevant nodes, queues, timers and callback state, not just printed business fields.','The Config.Clone omission is a separate sourced semantic discrepancy; no live protocol mutation or external consequence has been established from it.'],understanding='updated',rationale='Observed entry and transfer events answer reachability for the selected schedule. The rescue distinguishes missing initiation from unavailable quorum. Source review explains the misleading exported AutoLeave observation without suppressing it.',question_updates={c['id']:dict(unknowns=q['unknowns'],resume_conditions=[])}))\njson.dump(p,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 obligation.py\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));x=subprocess.run(r['validation']['command']+['submission.json'],capture_output=True,text=True);print(x.stdout,x.stderr)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
